"""IB DP History (new guide, first teaching 2026, first assessment 2028) – ib-g11-history.

Year 1 of the two-year course: historical thinking and the six key concepts, Paper 1 source skills
(prescribed focused studies Rwanda 1990–1994 and Kosovo 1989–1999), the authoritarian-rule theme
(Hitler, Mussolini, Mao, Castro), Paper 2 essay writing, historiography and the Historical
Investigation (IA).

Item styles
  * short knowledge items (define / identify / state) – C1,
  * explanation items (explain / distinguish / misconception) – C2,
  * application items: case-based explanation and Paper 1 source work (message, origin–purpose–
    content value and limitations) – C3,
  * Paper 1 compare-and-contrast and "using the sources and your own knowledge" synthesis, and
    Paper 2/3 essays (to what extent / evaluate / discuss / compare and contrast) with markbands – C4.
Source extracts are attributed; most are paraphrased or adapted from the named work and are labelled so.
"""
